# The fog run at the bow (rooms.ts, bow_fog). Wrong calls scrape the reef and loop back.
dialogue bearings
  node fog narrator "The fog closes over the bow like a lid. Somewhere aft, Quill has the wheel, and Dorrit stands halfway between us to pass the word."
    -> one
  node one narrator "The needle swings hard to the left of the bowsprit."
    > "“Port!”" -> oneOk
    > "“Starboard!”" -> oneBad
    > "“Left!”" -> left
  node left dorrit "He says LEFT! Is left a bearing?"
    -> left2
  node left2 vane "It is today! Port!"
    -> hail
  node oneBad dorrit "He says starboard!"
    -> oneBad2
  node oneBad2 hobb "He means port!"
    -> oneBad3
  node oneBad3 vane "He means whatever doesn't sink us!"
    -> oneScrape
  node oneScrape narrator "Something long and patient scrapes down the hull, from the bow to the stern, taking its time."
    -> oneRock
  node oneRock quill "That was a rock."
    -> one
  node oneOk quill "Port! Port it is!"
    -> hail
  node hail narrator "Out of the white to port, a voice through a speaking-trumpet, polite as a doorman: “Ahoy, the Marrow! Quarantine inspection! Heave to!”"
    -> hail2
  node hail2 narrator "It knows our name. Somewhere up a flight of wet steps in Port Vela, an old woman is saying: you don't answer."
    -> nobody
  node nobody vane "Weather. With a speaking-trumpet. Nobody answer it."
    -> astern
  node astern narrator "It falls astern, sounding hurt."
    -> two
  node two narrator "Dead ahead. The needle is perfectly still, and so is everyone."
    > "“Steady as she goes.”" -> twoOk
    > "“Port again!”" -> twoBad
    > "“Is anyone else's heart doing this?”" -> heart
  node heart hobb "Yes."
    -> two
  node twoBad dorrit "Port again, he says! Is that a request or a regulation?"
    -> twoBad2
  node twoBad2 vane "Port is where the rocks are, Mr Dorrit! Port is all rocks!"
    -> twoScrape
  node twoScrape narrator "The Marrow leans away from a rock close enough to sign for. Something in the galley breaks."
    -> twoRock
  node twoRock quill "Eyes on the needle, cargo! Not on the rocks. The rocks are my job."
    -> two
  node twoOk quill "Steady!"
    -> who
  node who vane "Who taught him that?"
    > "(Listen.)" if night_watch -> me
    > "(Listen.)" if not night_watch -> natural
  node me quill "Me. Last night."
    -> three
  node natural quill "Nobody. He reads it off a compass like it's a form. Don't tell him."
    -> three
  node three narrator "The needle leans a hair off the bowsprit, to the side I'd shake hands with. The rocks are close enough to read."
    > "“Starboard, a little.”" -> threeOk
    > "“Starboard, a lot!”" -> threeBad
  node threeBad hobb "How much is a lot?"
    -> threeBad2
  node threeBad2 vane "Less than that!"
    -> threeScrape
  node threeScrape narrator "The bowsprit swings past the gap and back again, like a man who's forgotten which door is his."
    -> three
  node threeOk quill "Good!"
    -> good
  node good quill "That was “good”, cargo. Write it down."
    > "Already written." -> lifts
    > "Underlined." -> lifts
      add aff 1
  node lifts narrator "The fog tears open like a curtain. Inside the reef: a lagoon as flat as glass, and a ship on the rocks, heeled over, masts up."
    -> flag
  node flag narrator "At her masthead, somebody has run up a flag made of shirts."
    -> vane
  node vane vane "That's a wreck. And somebody's still flying her colours."
    > "That's the Arcadia." -> arcadia
    > "(Look back at Quill.)" if aff >= 4 -> look
  node look narrator "At the wheel, Quill is looking at the wreck. Then, for one second, she's looking at me."
    > "That's the Arcadia." -> arcadia
  node arcadia fenn "…And shirts don't last three years in the weather. Somebody ran that up this week."
    -> alive
  node alive vane "Somebody's alive in there."
    -> smoke
  node smoke vane "And here's the fog, closing in behind her again. I'll not run the Marrow blind through that twice. We stand off outside the reef."
    -> boat
  node boat vane "Quill, take the boat in. Fenn: find out who's flying that rag, and run me up a new one I can steer by."
    -> sorry
  node sorry vane "If the old one's still up when the fog lifts, I'll assume you're both dead. And I'll be sorry."
    act 2
